<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Aydınoğlu Mehmed Bey</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1334</span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> · Also known as Mubariz al-Din Mehmed</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Aydınoğlu Mehmed Bey was a commander in the service of the Germiyanids who founded the Aydinid <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/beylik">beylik</a> in western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anatolia">Anatolia</a> around 1308. He conquered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/birgi">Birgi</a>, which became his capital, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ephesus">Ayasoluk</a> (Ephesus) and the upper citadel of Smyrna. His son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/umur-bey">Umur Bey</a> took the lower harbour fortress and built the fleets that raided the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aegean">Aegean</a>.</p></div>
